## 5. Structured Output Interceptor & LLM Repair Architecture

To guarantee 100% compliance with Zod schemas across all LLM sub-nodes:

```mermaid
graph TD
    SubNodeCall[Execute LLM Sub-Node Call] --> InterceptResponse[Capture Raw Text / JSON Response]
    InterceptResponse --> ZodValidate{Zod Schema SafeParse Success?}
    ZodValidate -- Yes --> ReturnState[Return Validated Partial State]
    ZodValidate -- No (Retry < 2) --> FormatErrorPrompt[Format LLM Repair Prompt with Exact Zod Issues]
    FormatErrorPrompt --> SubNodeCall
    ZodValidate -- No (Max Retries Reached) --> FallbackHandler[Trigger Safe Degradation / Partial State Recovery]
```

### Repair Prompt Strategy:
When `Zod.safeParse()` fails, the error interceptor automatically sends a repair prompt to the LLM:

```ts
export function buildRepairPrompt(rawResponse: string, zodError: z.ZodError): string {
  return `
YOUR PREVIOUS RESPONSE FAILED ZOD SCHEMA VALIDATION.

VALIDATION ERRORS:
${JSON.stringify(zodError.format(), null, 2)}

RAW PREVIOUS RESPONSE:
${rawResponse}

INSTRUCTIONS:
Fix the JSON payload to resolve ALL listed validation errors. Return ONLY valid JSON matching the schema.
`;
}
```

---

## 6. Tool Contracts & Deterministic TypeScript Helper Services

### 6.1 External LangChain Tools Contracts (7 Tools)
1. `gemini_web_search`: Gemini Google Search Grounding with citations.
2. `tavily_web_search`: Independent Tavily Search API.
3. `tavily_extract`: Deep full-page content extraction for high-value URLs.
4. `github_search_repositories`: GitHub REST repo search (`owner`, `name`, `stars`, `topics`).
5. `github_get_repository`: Detailed repository metadata.
6. `github_get_readme`: Raw decoded README fetching.
7. `github_get_contents`: Specific file fetching (`package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, etc.).

### 6.2 Deterministic Services Architecture
- **`webResearchService.ts`**: Executes `gemini_web_search` and `tavily_web_search` in parallel via `Promise.allSettled()`. Manages dual-search fallbacks.
- **`sourceNormalizer.ts`**: Removes tracking UTM params, trailing slashes, normalizes protocols.
- **`solutionDeduplicator.ts`**: Merges candidate references pointing to the same company/project/repo into 1 `DiscoveredSolution` with $N$ `sourceIds`.
- **`candidateRanker.ts`**: Scores candidate entities deterministically:
  $$\text{Score} = (\text{Relevance} \times 0.40) + (\text{Directness} \times 0.30) + (\text{Authority} \times 0.20) + (\text{Evidence} \times 0.10)$$
- **`evidenceMerger.ts`**: Combines evidence from multiple sources into a single solution object.

---

## 7. MongoDB Persistence, Caching & Real-Time SSE Events

### 7.1 Database Models
- `ResearchRun`: Persists execution metrics, stopping reasons, and complete `ResearchResult`.
- `SearchCache`: MongoDB query cache with 7-day TTL expiration index.
- `SourceRecord`: Normalized sources indexed by `canonicalUrl`.

### 7.2 Real-Time Event Stream (`GET /api/hackathons/:id/events`)
Sub-nodes emit real-time progress events for the frontend:
- `research_started`
- `discovery_queries_generated`
- `dual_search_executing`
- `sources_found`
- `candidates_ranked`
- `enrichment_started`
- `solution_enriched`
- `contradiction_detected`
- `research_completed`

---

## 8. Downstream Handshake with Agent 3 (Innovation Agent)

The complete `ResearchResult` payload passed to Agent 3 provides:
1. Clean, structured `discoveredSolutions` with concrete `features` (categorized & source-backed) and step-by-step `workflow` sequences.
2. Complete `sources` provenance list.
3. Summary metrics and unresolved research questions.

Agent 3 can immediately perform feature frequency analysis, workflow comparison, and gap detection without performing any external web searches.
